# Opus variant, classifier rename 2 of 5 (see README.md in this
# directory). Part of a matched set with the opus72 transplant in
# transplants.txt here: never apply the renames without it.
name: opus-rename-classifier-mod0-copy2
kind: module
module: 0
region: data
address: 0x030056F2
gate: Never apply without the opus72 transplant (patches/opus_swap/
  transplants.txt): the rename routes extension OPU to decoder
  module 72, which holds the WMA library until the transplant
  replaces it. Build refuses unless the 3 stock bytes at the target
  equal expect; the finished image must also pass
  firmware_patch.validate().
rationale: Second of three copies of the audio extension
  classifier string MP1MP2MP3WMAWAVAPEFLAAACM4AOGGMP43GPDFFDSF in
  module 0 data; the WMA entry sits at string offset +9. This copy
  is the one referenced by modules 22, 23, 27 (player), 31
  (browser) and 34. Renaming it to OPU makes slot 3 match the
  extension the FAT layer's 8.3 alias carries for .opus files, so
  Opus files reach decoder module 72 through the stock selection
  path, and .wma files stop matching.
expect: 574d41
replace: 4f5055
